        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-30T18:52:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about you define this as:\n```\npub fn hash(inputs: \u0026[\u0026[u8]]) -\u003e [u8; DIGEST_SIZE] {\n  let mut digest \u003d sha::Sha256::new();\n  inputs.iter().for_each(|in| digest.update(in));\n  digest.finish()\n}\n```\nand then you can use it more broadly, eg. lines 126-129 above become:\n```\nlet initrd_digest \u003d hash(\u0026[initrd, hash(\u0026[initrd_salt])]);\nassert_eq!(initrd_digest, verified_data.initrd_digest, \"...\");\n```",
